  `cu<=ru+2` fits this class and is 17/31 and 17/29 on GRID M's
  SELF-1B and LOAD, so it is a CLAUSE and not a rule — and it is
  scored here, never proposed.  No successor is fitted on the cells
  that refuted its predecessor (w-ilx's standing instruction).

  The axes NONE of the four lanes varied, which is what a SELF-2B
  grid owes first:
    * the bind's own DISPLACEMENT (all five families bind at one)
    * the DEPTH of the value's path (`&s->mid` vs `&s->mid.in1`)
    * whether the path's TAIL agrees with the store's
    * cu = ru+2 AND cu = ru+3 in the same family (only w-spell H
      and GRID M reach either, and neither reaches both)
